{"conversation":"Hmm, I realize that s.count(sub) doesn't count overlapping occurrences, so if the special substring repeats within the string with overlaps, like "aaa" containing "aa" twice overlapping, this method won't count properly. So I need another way to count occurrences that include overlaps.","python_code":"class Solution:
    def maximumLength(self, s: str) -> int:
        max_len = -1
        n = len(s)
        for length in range(1, n+1):
            for i in range(n-length+1):
                sub = s[i:i+length]
                if len(set(sub)) == 1:
                    count = 0
